,"choiceReasons":{"A":"Which normally refers to things, not this person.","B":"Whose needs a following noun to express possession.","C":"Where would express a place role, not the person subject.","D":"**Who** refers to the person and is the subject of the relative clause."}}},{"id":"4ee1d506-d029-5902-ac87-fce29a045354","topicSlug":"relative-clauses","level":"B1","prompt":"Add extra information: “Our assistant, ____ prepares the evening meal every week, is away.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"—"},{"id":"B","text":"whose"},{"id":"C","text":"who"},{"id":"D","text":"that"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The **commas** signal extra information, and the referent is a person.","explanation":"The commas mark a non-defining clause about a person, so use **who**.","keywords":["nondefining-relative"],"skill":"nondefining-relative","contextKey":"relative-clauses-49","fingerprint":"83a6ed1127baa12b28aa54891c59836d86bb937b1b2827a405112c14b8a235bb","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-relative"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The **commas** signal extra information, and the referent is a person.","The commas mark a non-defining clause about a person, so use **who**.","Choose **who**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The pronoun cannot be omitted in a non-defining clause.","B":"Whose requires a noun after it to express possession.","C":"The commas mark a non-defining clause about a person, so use **who**.","D":"That is not used as the relative pronoun in an ordinary non-defining clause."}}},{"id":"574ead8c-c70e-519d-a5c3-af09aabeaf1c","topicSlug":"relative-clauses","level":"B1","prompt":"Express possession: “The assistant ____ job is to prepare the evening meal has arrived.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"whose"},{"id":"B","text":"who"},{"id":"C","text":"who’s"},{"id":"D","text":"which"}],"